-- title:
--   Zero-scheme ideal of c Ω on affine opens
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and $N$ a sheaf of modules on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ for which the pullback of $N$ along the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit module of $U$. Let $V \subseteq X$ be open and let $\Omega \in \Gamma(N, V)$ satisfy `IsFrameOn \Omega V`, i.e. for every open $W \le V$ the map $g \mapsto g \cdot (\Omega|_W)$ from $\Gamma(X, W)$ to $\Gamma(N, W)$ is bijective. Let $\sigma$ be a morphism of modules from the unit $\mathbf{1}_{X\text{-Mod}}$ to $N$, and let $c \in \Gamma(X, V)$ be such that the value of $\sigma$ over $V$ at the section $1 \in \Gamma(X,V)$, viewed in the unit module via `toUnitSection`, equals $c \cdot \Omega$. Then for every affine open $U$ of $X$ with $U \le V$, the ideal at $U$ of the ideal sheaf data `zeroSchemeIdeal \sigma` — the infimum of all ideal sheaf data $J$ on $X$ with $\mathrm{coeffIdeal}(\sigma, W) \le J.\mathrm{ideal}\,W$ for every affine open $W$, where $\mathrm{coeffIdeal}(\sigma, W)$ is the ideal of $\Gamma(X, W)$ spanned by the range of `Scheme.Modules.coeff \sigma W` — is the principal ideal of $\Gamma(X, U)$ generated by the restriction of $c$ to $U$.
--
--   This is the local description of the zero scheme of a section of an invertible module: over an affine open contained in a trivialising open, the vanishing ideal sheaf is generated by the coefficient of the section with respect to the frame. It feeds into [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.nonempty_iso_of_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.nonempty_iso_of_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq), where equality of zero-scheme ideals is turned into an isomorphism of invertible modules.
